  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe AI Assistant's `execute_sql_query` tool accepted multi-statement payloads. A single `COMMIT; <write-statement>; SELECT 1` string terminated the enclosing `BEGIN TRANSACTION READ ONLY` wrapper and ran subsequent statements in autocommit mode. On a superuser-connected session this chains to operating-system command execution on the database host via `COPY ... TO PROGRAM`.\n\nThe fix rejects any query that contains more than one statement and verifies that each query is a read-only `SELECT`.\n\n## Affected versions\n\npgAdmin 4 **>= 9.13, < 9.16**\n\n## Fix\n\nFixed in pgAdmin 4 **9.16** by commit [`bf4792444`](https://github.com/pgadmin-org/pgadmin4/commit/bf4792444).\n\n## Severity\n\n- CVSS 3.1: **9.0 CRITICAL** — `CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H`\n- CVSS 4.0: **9.4 CRITICAL** — `CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H`\n\n## Credit\n\nReported by **Isaac Chen**.\n\n## References\n\n- CVE: [CVE-2026-12045](https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-12045)\n- Release notes: [pgAdmin 4 9.16](https://github.com/pgadmin-org/pgadmin4/blob/REL-9_16/docs/en_US/release_notes_9_16.rst)",
